<article class="env-exercise" id="029L">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/029L">Exercise <span data-tag="029L">111.35.10</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of schemes over $S$. Let $x \in X$ be a point. Set $y = f(x)$. Assume that the natural map $\kappa (y) \to \kappa (x)$ is bijective. Show, using the definition, that $f$ induces a natural linear map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \text{d}f : T_{X/S, x} \longrightarrow T_{Y/S, y}.  \]
</div>
  <p> Match it with what happens on local rings via Exercise <a href="/tag/029E" data-tag="029E">111.35.2</a> in case $\kappa (x) = \kappa (s)$. </p>
</article>